<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Privileged permission allowlist for com.qualcomm.qti.telephonyservice, the
    stock QTI app whose QcRilAudioHidl class is the client for
    vendor.qti.hardware.radio.am@1.0::IQcRilAudio. Optional: the build ships
    QcRilAm instead. See scripts/extract-qti-telephony.sh and docs/23-volte.md.

    WHY THIS FILE IS NEEDED AT ALL

    Stock installs the APK to /system_ext/app, unprivileged, and it works there
    because it is signed with Onyx's platform key and MODIFY_AUDIO_ROUTING is
    signature|privileged. Our build has a different platform key, so the
    signature half never matches and the app must earn the permission through
    the privileged half instead. That means /system_ext/priv-app plus this
    allowlist.

    Without it, AudioManager.setAudioServerStateCallback throws

        SecurityException: Not allowed to monitor audioserver state

    inside AudioController's constructor. The field stays null, onCreate hits a
    NullPointerException at QtiTelephonyService.java:109, and because the app is
    android:persistent the framework restarts it forever.

    Only MODIFY_AUDIO_ROUTING is listed. The app's other two permissions,
    MODIFY_AUDIO_SETTINGS and RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED, are normal and granted on
    install.

    NOTE ON XML COMMENTS: a literal double hyphen anywhere in a comment makes
    this file unparseable. SystemConfig then drops the whole block while still
    logging that it read the file, PackageManager throws at boot, and the device
    loops. That cost one boot loop already. Validate with
    scripts/check-device-xml.py before installing.
-->
<permissions>
    <privapp-permissions package="com.qualcomm.qti.telephonyservice">
        <permission name="android.permission.MODIFY_AUDIO_ROUTING"/>
    </privapp-permissions>
</permissions>
